#: ../../src/signal.rst:5
msgid ":c:type:`uv_signal_t` --- Signal handle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/signal.rst:7
msgid ""
"Signal handles implement Unix style signal handling on a per-event loop "
"bases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/signal.rst:10
msgid "Windows notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/signal.rst:12
msgid "Reception of some signals is emulated:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/signal.rst:14
msgid ""
"SIGINT is normally delivered when the user presses CTRL+C. However, like "
"on Unix, it is not generated when terminal raw mode is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/signal.rst:17
msgid "SIGBREAK is delivered when the user pressed CTRL + BREAK."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/signal.rst:19
msgid ""
"SIGHUP is generated when the user closes the console window. On SIGHUP "
"the program is given approximately 10 seconds to perform cleanup. After "
"that Windows will unconditionally terminate it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/signal.rst:23
msgid ""
"SIGWINCH is raised whenever libuv detects that the console has been "
"resized. When a libuv app is running under a console emulator, or when a "
"32-bit libuv app is running on 64-bit system, SIGWINCH will be emulated. "
"In such cases SIGWINCH signals may not always be delivered in a timely "
"manner. For a writable :c:type:`uv_tty_t` handle libuv will only detect "
"size changes when the cursor is moved. When a readable :c:type:`uv_tty_t`"
" handle is used, resizing of the console buffer will be detected only if "
"the handle is in raw mode and is being read."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/signal.rst:32
msgid ""
"Watchers for other signals can be successfully created, but these signals"
" are never received. These signals are: `SIGILL`, `SIGABRT`, `SIGFPE`, "
"`SIGSEGV`, `SIGTERM` and `SIGKILL.`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/signal.rst:36
msgid ""
"Calls to raise() or abort() to programmatically raise a signal are not "
"detected by libuv; these will not trigger a signal watcher."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/signal.rst:39
msgid "SIGWINCH support on Windows was improved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/signal.rst:40
msgid ""
"32-bit libuv SIGWINCH support on 64-bit Windows was rolled back to old "
"implementation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/signal.rst:44
msgid "Unix notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/signal.rst:46
msgid "SIGKILL and SIGSTOP are impossible to catch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/signal.rst:48
msgid ""
"Handling SIGBUS, SIGFPE, SIGILL or SIGSEGV via libuv results into "
"undefined behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/signal.rst:50
msgid ""
"SIGABRT will not be caught by libuv if generated by `abort()`, e.g. "
"through `assert()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/signal.rst:52
msgid ""
"On Linux SIGRT0 and SIGRT1 (signals 32 and 33) are used by the NPTL "
"pthreads library to manage threads. Installing watchers for those signals"
" will lead to unpredictable behavior and is strongly discouraged. Future "
"versions of libuv may simply reject them."
msgstr ""

